 "capsule": "The Aq Qoyunlu ('White Sheep' Turkmen) were a Sunni Turkoman tribal confederation founded in 1378 by Qara Yuluk Uthman Beg in the Diyarbakır region of eastern Anatolia. Under Uzun Hasan (r. 1453–1478) they crushed the rival Kara Koyunlu and Timurid remnants to build an empire stretching across eastern Anatolia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Iraq, and much of Iran, ruling from Tabriz. Succession wars fragmented the confederation after 1497, and the rising Safavid dynasty under Shah Ismail I extinguished the last Aq Qoyunlu claimants in the early 1500s.",
